  "class_description": "Definition:\nZone seaward of the lowest tide limit.\nThis class is applicable for:\n- bays;\n- fjords or fjards, sea lochs, ryas and straits;\n- sea surface below lowest tide limit;\n- off-shore floating aquaculture facilities for fish, shellfish or macroalgae production.\nThis class includes:\n- sea water;\n- floating marine vegetation (macroalgae);\n- floating aquaculture installations, such as cages, tanks, buoy lines;\n- narrow (<100 m wide) coast defence structures (breakwaters, seawalls, sea dikes, groins, jetties) stretching into the sea.\nThis class is not applicable for:\n- archipelago of lands located inside sea/ocean areas;\n- sea water areas as part of port areas that include sea water to reach a zone > 25 ha (class 123);\n- on-shore aquaculture installations, such as tanks, basins, buildings (class 121).\nThis class excludes:\n-",
